Appendix G: Self‑Model Router and Total Loss

G.1 Differentiable Router

The self‑model router outputs a probability distribution over geometries \alpha \in \Delta^{|\mathcal{G}|} given a query z_{\text{query}} and core state z_{\text{core}}:

\alpha = \operatorname{Softmax}\left( \frac{\operatorname{MLP}([z_{\text{query}}; z_{\text{core}}])}{\tau} \right).

The final prediction is

\hat{y} = \sum_{i \in \mathcal{G}} \alpha_i \cdot \text{decoder}_i(z_i).

The entropy regularization is

\mathcal{L}_{\text{ent}} = \sum_{i \in \mathcal{G}} \alpha_i \log \alpha_i,

which encourages exploration. An annealing schedule is used for the weight \lambda_{\text{ent}} to allow specialization.

G.2 Overall Training Objective

The total loss is:

\mathcal{L}_{\text{total}} = \mathcal{L}_{\text{task}} + \lambda_1 \mathcal{L}_{\text{CGC}} + \lambda_2 \mathcal{L}_{\text{causal}} + \lambda_3 \mathcal{L}_{\text{ent}} + \lambda_4 \mathcal{L}_{\text{reg}} + \lambda_5 \mathcal{L}_{\text{local}},

where:

· \mathcal{L}_{\text{task}} is the cross‑entropy loss for the counterfactual question.
· \mathcal{L}_{\text{CGC}} is the scale‑normalized star‑topology consistency loss.
· \mathcal{L}_{\text{causal}} includes reconstruction, intervention prediction, and DAG constraint for G_C.
· \mathcal{L}_{\text{ent}} is the entropy regularization from the router.
· \mathcal{L}_{\text{reg}} is the VICReg regularization.
· \mathcal{L}_{\text{local}} is the local neighborhood preservation loss.

All terms are differentiable and trained end‑to‑end.

